<title>UK: EU Commissioner says Japan interested in euro zone.</title>
<headline>EU Commissioner says Japan interested in euro zone.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union monetary affairs Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said on Thursday Japanese businessmen were interested in Europe's single currency zone.</p>
<p>De Silguy said he had spoken to a group of Japanese businessmen just prior to Toyota's statement a week ago it was reconsidering its future investment decisions in Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;They said they were very interested in having a euro zone with a sound economy to put their savings,&quot; De Silguy told reporters. He was in London for a series of meetings with British financial authorities and industry leaders.</p>
<p>-- Jennifer Scott, London newsroom +44 171 542 8682</p>
